@*
    The one confirmation that throws the working copy away, wherever it is asked from.

    Discarding is confirmed, and staging and applying-a-draft are not, which is the opposite way round
    from the usual reflex — deliberately. Every edit up to here wrote to a draft and touched no table,
    so staging one needs no ceremony; this is the only control that destroys work the operator did, and
    the one that cannot be undone. So it looks like what it does — the danger button, with a Cancel
    beside it — rather than the green of every safe action on the screen. An AlvoConfirm: centred, no
    light dismiss, Escape = Cancel (spec §3.2).

    One component because there are two ways in, Preview and the shell's pending bar, and two copies of
    a destructive confirmation are two chances for one of them to drift back to green.
*@
@inject AdminSession Session
@inject ISnackbar Snackbar

<AlvoConfirm Open="Open" TestId="discard-sheet" ConfirmTestId="discard-confirm" CancelTestId="discard-cancel"
             Title="Discard every unapplied change?"
             Consequence="@($"The working copy goes back to revision {_revision}. There is no undo.")"
             Verb="Discard changes" OnConfirm="DiscardAsync" OnCancel="OnClose" />

@code {
    private int _revision;

    /// <summary>Whether the confirmation is on the page.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public bool Open { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Raised when the operator backs out — Cancel or Escape.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback OnClose { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Raised after the copy went back to the applied revision.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback OnDiscarded { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Reads the revision the copy would go back to, each time the confirm opens.</summary>
    protected override async Task OnParametersSetAsync()
    {
        if (Open)
        {
            _revision = (await Session.CopyAsync(CancellationToken.None)).Revision;
        }
    }

    private async Task DiscardAsync()
    {
        (await Session.CopyAsync(CancellationToken.None)).Discard();
        Snackbar.Confirm("Discarded the working copy");
        await OnDiscarded.InvokeAsync();
    }
}
